  <data key="d0">Monoclonal Antibody Chromatography Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monoclonal Antibody Chromatography Protocol is a purification process for therapeutic IgG antibodies, primarily utilizing protein A affinity chromatography. It is also referred to as a chromatography technique, method, and high-throughput purification protocol. Additionally, it is termed an affinity chromatography method and an antibody purification method.</data>
