  <data key="d0">t-SNE</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">t-Distributed Stochastic Neighbor Embedding (t-SNE) is a method used for visualizing high-dimensional data in 2D or 3D, focusing on local structure rather than global variance.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b7bb64c7c77afa990b98fea6bfe6daa</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742849</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Latent Space">
  <data key="d0">Latent Space</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Latent space refers to the space in which hidden or abstract features of the data are represented, allowing for interpolation and visualization of latent variables.&lt;SEP&gt;Latent space refers to the abstract space used by generative models for representing the parameters of a probability distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6b7bb64c7c77afa990b98fea6bfe6daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcdf9fb2be50ad48fc943fd5744a44c7</data>
