  <data key="d0">Adapters</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Adapters are small trainable feed-forward layers inserted inside Transformer attention or feed-forward blocks to keep main parameters frozen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional Prompting &amp; Attribute Tokens">
  <data key="d0">Conditional Prompting &amp; Attribute Tokens</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditional prompting involves prepending control tokens to the tokenized sequence during training and fine-tuning to specify specific attributes like tempo, instrumentation, key signature, and genre identity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loss Weighting &amp; Stylistic Regularization">
  <data key="d0">Loss Weighting &amp; Stylistic Regularization</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss weighting and stylistic regularization techniques include adding penalty terms to the negative log-likelihood loss to ensure adherence to genre-specific rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Copyright &amp; Training Data Ownership">
  <data key="d0">Copyright &amp; Training Data Ownership</data>
  <data key="d1">issue</data>
  <data key="d2">Training models on protected musical works without explicit licenses raises concerns about copyright infringement and fair use.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vocal Cloning &amp; Right of Publicity">
  <data key="d0">Vocal Cloning &amp; Right of Publicity</data>
  <data key="d1">issue</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthesizing recognizable vocal timbres from real artists poses ethical risks regarding consent and misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribution, Watermarking &amp; Watermark Detection">
  <data key="d0">Attribution, Watermarking &amp; Watermark Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">issue</data>
  <data key="d2">Embedding imperceptible watermarks in generated music files to ensure provenance and prevent deceptive uploads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cultural Diversity vs. Bias">
  <data key="d0">Cultural Diversity vs. Bias</data>
  <data key="d1">issue</data>
  <data key="d2">Dominant training sets in AI-generated music tend to favor Western traditions, limiting native support for microtonal systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core Concepts">
  <data key="d0">Core Concepts</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer learning is a technique that leverages pre-training and fine-tuning approaches to adapt generative models to specific domains.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="human performance">
  <data key="d0">human performance</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6135cb11db83854564319c8740d39c</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-time inputs are used to enhance human performance during accompaniment and production.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="model latent spaces">
  <data key="d0">model latent spaces</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a6135cb11db83854564319c8740d39c</data>
  <data key="d2">Controllable latent spaces enable the manipulation of musical attributes like melody, harmony, rhythm, timbre, and dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Techniques">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Techniques</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer learning is a core concept evolving into advanced techniques such as real-time audio synthesis and neural audio codecs.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Emerging Trends">
  <data key="d0">Emerging Trends</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer learning is a technique that is developing into emerging trends like real-time interactive co-creation and latent spaces for music synthesis.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ethical Considerations">
  <data key="d0">Ethical Considerations</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer learning introduces challenges like copyright infringement, vocal cloning risks, and bias in cultural diversity.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Future Directions">
  <data key="d0">Future Directions</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethical considerations are intertwined with the evolution of future AI-driven music generation technologies.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technological Evolution">
  <data key="d0">Technological Evolution</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-99f8fa13cb484b51ce51ba03554bbc27</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethical considerations drive the evolution of AI-driven music generation, leading to paradigm shifts in methodologies and techniques.</data>
  <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-5.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742979</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UNIT-IV">
  <data key="d0">UNIT-IV</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">UNIT-IV focuses on Music Generation using Generative AI.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Music Generation">
  <data key="d0">Music Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Music generation involves capturing temporal dynamics, harmonic structures, and polyphonic dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MIDI">
  <data key="d0">MIDI</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MIDI represents musical events symbolically and records them as discrete sequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Piano Roll Representation">
  <data key="d0">Piano Roll Representation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Piano Roll Representation visualizes music as a 2D binary matrix with time steps and pitch dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM-Based Music Generation">
  <data key="d0">LSTM-Based Music Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">LSTMs process music as temporal sequences by maintaining a persistent cell state for learning long-term patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transformer-Based Music Generation">
  <data key="d0">Transformer-Based Music Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Transformer architectures process long sequences in parallel to capture multi-bar themes and harmonic structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Causal Transformer Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Causal Transformer Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Causal Transformer Architecture maintains an autoregressive generation pipeline by using causal self-attention.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3fc8a2ebcc1e39fbd3ba48d67f7f264d</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MuseGAN">
  <data key="d0">MuseGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MuseGAN is a method for generating polyphonic music compositions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MIDI Dataset">
  <data key="d0">MIDI Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Lakh MIDI Dataset is used for training MuseGAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symbolic Music Datasets">
  <data key="d0">Symbolic Music Datasets</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Symbolic Music Datasets are converted into multi-track piano-roll tensors for training.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sigmoid">
  <data key="d0">Sigmoid</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sigmoid is used as an activation function in generating layers of MuseGAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wasserstein GAN">
  <data key="d0">Wasserstein GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wasserstein GAN is used to optimize the training of multi-track GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Penalty (WGAN-GP)">
  <data key="d0">Gradient Penalty (WGAN-GP)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gradient Penalty (WGAN-GP) is used to handle training instability in multi-track GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="3D Transposed Convolutions">
  <data key="d0">3D Transposed Convolutions</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">3D Transposed Convolutions are used to expand temporal dimensions for multi-bar generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyphonic Music Datasets">
  <data key="d0">Polyphonic Music Datasets</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyphonic Music Datasets are used for training MuseGAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lakh MIDI Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Lakh MIDI Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The Lakh MIDI Dataset is a specific polyphonic music dataset used for training MuseGAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f962918487ef320fd45d2de09dceac4</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Positional Encodings">
  <data key="d0">Positional Encodings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Positional encodings are used to inject structural relationships based on the distance between notes, preserving musical motifs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Standard Absolute Positional Encodings">
  <data key="d0">Standard Absolute Positional Encodings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard absolute positional encodings struggle with musical concepts such as key transpositions or repeating rhythm motifs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relative Positional Encodings">
  <data key="d0">Relative Positional Encodings</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Relative Positional Encodings are a modification of standard encodings that maintain musical motifs regardless of their position in a piece.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pitch Class Histogram Distance">
  <data key="d0">Pitch Class Histogram Distance</data>
  <data key="d1">evaluation_metric</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures KL divergence between the distribution of 12 chromatic pitch classes in generated music and a target dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scale Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Scale Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">evaluation_metric</data>
  <data key="d2">Calculates the ratio of generated notes that fit within a dominant musical scale (e.g., C Major).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Empty Bar Rate (EBR)">
  <data key="d0">Empty Bar Rate (EBR)</data>
  <data key="d1">evaluation_metric</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures the percentage of generated bars that contain no active note events.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polyphonic Density">
  <data key="d0">Polyphonic Density</data>
  <data key="d1">evaluation_metric</data>
  <data key="d2">Calculates the average number of simultaneous active notes per bar or beat.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Perplexity (PPL)">
  <data key="d0">Perplexity (PPL)</data>
  <data key="d1">evaluation_metric</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures how well an autoregressive model predicts unseen test MIDI event sequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-140833bd08793c8ef46f4afbc10aa877</data>
  <data key="d4">GA-Unit-4.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1793742989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
